// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§6.6", "§4.6", "§6.3", "§18.1"]

// S-138, S-70, X23-8 (W5-04 U1; the first-period form): a hand-written `impl Drop for Ty` is the E0200 of the form
// in this version (§18.1: "形の全体がこの版に無いもの(`impl Tr for P`…)は形の E0200 で、中の名前を読まない"; S-138; the
// second period opens it, tasks/phase2.md). The impl is not read, so the type has no `Drop` implementation and its kind is
// the one of its structure (§4.6: Copy for a struct of Copy fields), and a `const` of the type, or of a type that holds
// it, is right: there is no E0407 from the failed impl (a result of a stage that failed is not a premise of the
// next, §18.1). The E0407 of a `Drop` type (§4.6: "Affine = `Buf`、`Drop` 実装型") is in the second period. The E0407 of
// the types that are Affine by their structure is in negative/const_type_affine_position.onsa. The only error of
// the file is the E0200.
pub struct Handle {
  id: U32,
}

impl Drop for Handle {                          //~ E0200
  rt fn drop(move self) {}
}

pub struct Pair {
  first: Handle,
  second: U32,
}

const RESOURCE: Handle = Handle { id: 1 }

const WRAPPED: Pair = Pair { first: Handle { id: 2 }, second: 3 }

impl Handle {
  const SPARE: Handle = Handle { id: 0 }
}
